    Founder directive: Ministry of Economy, obligation expiry, proceed-by-default, dispatch gate, daily plenary
    
    Act 29 (Ministry of Economy, Executive office c1e00012): keeps the Antonina
    model list in tier order free -> contributor -> paid -> Luna last, adds only
    free models that answered a probe, restores the previous config if Antonina
    rejects the new list, and never writes an empty list. Judgment (prefer and
    exclude within a tier) comes from state/economy/model-policy.json; the tier
    table is code. Funding risk is reported from live host-wide cooldowns.
    
    Act 30 (ordinary law, not a constitutional change):
    - obligation-expiry.py: stale reconciliation receipts, open handoffs and
      Judiciary mailbox items expire after 72h unless renewed with a reason;
      nothing is deleted, expired receipts are marked unverified.
    - proceed-by-default.sh: a reversible request unanswered after its deadline
      (24h default, 72h max) lets the requester proceed; the addressee audits
      afterwards; irreversible acts never proceed by default.
    - dispatch-gate.sh: Executive, Judiciary, Recovery Steward, Clerk and the
      Ministry skip the model call when every input is unchanged, with a periodic
      heartbeat; failed launches never record a pass; the gate fails open.
    - daily-sitting.py: Parliament sits once per UTC day so a quorum can form;
      it releases the seats it summoned and never touches the Clerk's summonses.
    - daily digest stays ten lines; line 10 now shows inaction as a cost.
    - AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY items 6-11 including standing bounded chores.
    
    Adds smoke tests for each new mechanism and the Ministry cycle; the full
    suite passes under dash.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
